Languages

.system of responsibilities 




.data definition language - structure - build the world 
    .creates and shapes the structure of the database 
        .CREATE, ALTER, DROP, CREATE INDEX 
    .use when designing schemas, adding columns, or restructuring data models 


.data manipulation language - day to day operations - work inside the world 
    .inserts, updates, deletes, and retrieves data 
        .SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE 


.data query language - reading data with precision - work inside the world 
    .pure querying 
        .SELECT 
    .filtering, sorting, grouping, joining, and extracting insights 


.data control language - who can do that - protect the world 
    .permissions and security 
        .GRANT, REVOKE 
    .DBAs and engineers use it to manage access control 


.transaction control language - safety and consistency - keep the world consistent 
    .manage transactions and ensure data integrity 
        .COMMIT, ROLLBACK, SAVEPOINT 
    .critical in systems where data accuracy matters e.g healthcare, logistics, finance 

 